# Deep chains of closures freed whole (Phase 2 on l2r-base7: upstream Reussir frees a closure enum whose variant has a
# managed field after its recursive one, or two recursive fields, with its destructor executor, which keeps a frame per
# level: at 10^6 levels `big` peaked at 652 MB, `comp` at 156 MB, native 102 MB and 86 MB; dev with the old drop patches
# 68 MB and 46 MB). Peak memory at 10^6 within native's plus 4000 KB; allocations and bytes as native's.
big 250000 | big 1000000 | 1 2000 | rss 1 4000
bigu 250000 | bigu 1000000 | 1 2000 | rss 1 4000
bigt 250000 | bigt 1000000 | 1 2000 | rss 1 4000
comp 250000 | comp 1000000 | 1 2000 | rss 1 4000
small 250000 | small 1000000 | 1 2000 | rss 1 4000
smallu 250000 | smallu 1000000 | 1 2000 | rss 1 4000
list 250000 | list 1000000 | 1 2000 | rss 1 4000
